sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Sc as Scanner
    participant FS as Filesystem
    participant Idx as Hash index
    Sc->>FS: walk the tree
    FS-->>Sc: paths and sizes
    Sc->>Sc: group by size first
    Note over Sc: only files of identical size can be duplicates — this removes most candidates for free
    Sc->>FS: read a small prefix of each candidate
    Sc->>Sc: cheap prefix hash to split the group further
    Sc->>FS: full content hash on what survives
    Sc->>Idx: record hash to paths
    alt hashes match
        Sc->>FS: compare byte for byte before acting
        Note over Sc,FS: never delete on a hash alone — and re-stat, because the file may have changed since you walked it
    end
